Version 0.1(Basic Spiking Neural Network (SNN))
Architecture:
Conv1 (3→16) → LIF → MaxPool → Conv2 (16→32) → LIF → MaxPool → FC1 (8192→128) → LIF → FC2 (128→6) → LIF

Ismein 2 convolutional layers hain. Har convolution ke baad LIF neuron aur pooling use ho rahi hai. Output layer 6 diseases represent karti hai.

Version 0.2(Multimodal Spiking VGG-13)
Version 0.2 mein humne architecture ko considerably expand kiya. Sabse pehla major change ye tha ke ab humne MILK10k dataset ki saari 11 classes include 
kar li aur single modality ke bajaye dual-modality approach introduce ki, jisme dermoscopic aur clinical close-up images dono use ho rahi thi. 
Iske liye humne dual-branch Spiking VGG-13 architecture implement kiya, jahan dono images separate branches se process hoti hain aur unke extracted 
features baad mein concatenate kiye jate hain. Har branch mein 10 convolutional layers, spiking neurons aur average pooling use hui. Input image ka 
size 128 × 128 tha, aur har branch se 32,768 features extract ho rahe the. Dono branches ko combine karne ke baad 65,536 features fully connected layer 
mein ja rahe the. Is version mein humne latency encoding ki jagah Bernoulli rate encoding use ki, jisme pixel intensity spike generate hone ki probability 
determine karti hai. Neuron ka beta 1.0 rakha gaya tha, jis se neuron IF-like behavior show karta tha, yani membrane potential mein leakage nahi hoti thi. 
Training ke liye Adam optimizer, class-balanced focal loss aur weighted sampling introduce ki gayi taake class imbalance handle ho sake. Lekin training ke 
results satisfactory nahi the. Validation accuracy approximately 5.85% thi aur model almost saari images ko AKIEC class mein classify kar raha tha. Iska major 
diagnostic issue ye tha ke final output layer meaningful spikes generate nahi kar rahi thi. Isliye architecture zyada advanced hone ke bawajood model effectively 
learn nahi kar raha tha.
